	(text "100 Ω differential pairs; P on the transformer's - ends, N on its + ends, both sides (see the layout)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 189.23 201.93 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.85 0.85)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "fce63e5e-5b88-826e-8160-20ba09846956")
	)
	(text_box "+3V3_ETH is +3V3 through a ferrite bead (power sheet).\nPHY address strap at its default (RXD3 pulled up internally): PHYAD = 1.\nRXD1 pulled up (4.7 k): TXDLY = 1; RXD0 at its internal pull-up: RXDLY = 1:\nboth 2 ns RGMII delays inside the PHY, so the gateware adds none (LiteEth tx_delay = rx_delay = 0)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 330.2 335.28 0)
		(size 87.63 8.89)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 194 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.95 0.95)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "4378555d-5baa-dc78-df3b-e307d1220fb4")
	)
	(text_box "The FPGA talks RGMII (4-bit DDR at 125 MHz) at 3.3 V to the PHY, through 22 Ω series resistors.\nThe PHY makes its own 1.0 V core with an internal switcher (REG_OUT, 2.2 µH).\nStraps on the LED and RXD pins are sampled at reset: CFG_EXT = 1 (external 3.3 V on DVDD_RG),\nCFG_LDO[1:0] = 00 (3.3 V I/O pads), PHY address 1, both RGMII delays inside the PHY (TXDLY = RXDLY = 1).\nThe magnetics are a G2406S module: each chip-side centre tap gets its own 100 nF to ground;\nthe line-side taps go to a Bob Smith termination (75 Ω each, 1 nF / 3 kV 1812 to ground)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 25.4 0)
		(size 109.22 13.97)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type default)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 255 194 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "fedb86bf-910e-ef94-be58-73e17360988b")
	)
